    "extraction_notes": [
      "Supplied PDF SHA-256 verified as 54add4ec6272851e0e7617457eae2ee8742aa6ad1d3bae43660e5ddada67cbe8.",
      "Fig. 3 solid ES1AW-ES1DW typical forward-voltage curve explicitly includes ES1DW. The listed points are direct observations from the supplied vector plot at Tj = 25 degC, pulse width = 300 us, and 1% duty cycle; no intermediate points were synthesized.",
      "Fig. 4 typical reverse-characteristics curves were digitized at Tj = 25 degC and Tj = 125 degC. Reverse-current values are represented as positive magnitudes because the plotted axis is instantaneous reverse current in uA.",
      "The electrical-characteristics table gives maximum VF = 1.0 V at IF = 1.0 A for the ES1AW-ES1DW group, maximum Trr = 35 ns at IF = 0.5 A, IR = 1.0 A, and Irr = 0.25 A, maximum IR1 = 2.0 uA at VR = VDC = 200 V and Ta = 25 degC, maximum IR2 = 200 uA at Ta = 125 degC, and typical CJ = 7.0 pF at 4.0 V DC and 1 MHz.",
      "Absolute-rating bounds for ES1DW are VRRM = 200 V, VRMS = 140 V, VDC = 200 V, IF(AV) = 1.0 A, and IFSM = 30.0 A at Ta = 25 degC; junction and storage temperature ratings are -55 to +150 degC. These ratings are limits, not fitted curve points.",
      "The datasheet publishes no breakdown-voltage or breakdown-current specification; VRRM and VDC ratings are not treated as breakdown data."
    ],
